cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Topological Validation Pipeline
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself
  and the preprint it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Garví-Gualda
    given-names: Jesús
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-9061-1087"
    affiliation: Universidad de Murcia
    email: jesus.garvig@um.es
repository-code: "https://github.com/j-garvi/topological-validation"
abstract: >-
  A post-hoc validation tool that uses sublevel-set persistent
  homology to detect structural hallucinations in reconstructed
  2D scalar fields. It reports RMSE alongside a reduced H0
  feature count and the Wasserstein-2 distance between
  persistence diagrams, which separates reconstructions that
  pointwise metrics rank as comparable.
keywords:
  - persistent homology
  - topological data analysis
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - computational validation
  - Navier-Stokes equations
license: MIT
